[{:db/id 17592186129263 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-abc95782-56f0-5602-a797-77bbd8bc8d07"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-abc95782-56f0-5602-a797-77bbd8bc8d07" :question/id #uuid "abc95782-56f0-5602-a797-77bbd8bc8d07" :question/math-academy-id "q-160382" :question/problem "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT([\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}])⟶[\\begin{aligned}uv \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{u}{v})\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n  \n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x=uv$ and $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{u}{v}).$ \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =u \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =\\frac{1}{u} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-\\frac{1}{v}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}v & u \\\\ \\frac{1}{u} & -\\frac{1}{v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =v\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{v})-u\\cdot \\frac{1}{u} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,3)}=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-59271587-d957-593c-984d-f14328120bc0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-59271587-d957-593c-984d-f14328120bc0" :answer-field/id #uuid "59271587-d957-593c-984d-f14328120bc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3c97f35c-4480-5e3e-a894-f3effca05b9b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3c97f35c-4480-5e3e-a894-f3effca05b9b" "answer-375f59e1-b6c5-51a0-ad58-23511b54c59d" "answer-cc31709a-e3d1-56b4-9a97-dea545336cc4" "answer-5959bb5d-4929-5707-80e3-51ab7b1c379f" "answer-2f9115f7-c967-552e-babd-64a7c492372a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c97f35c-4480-5e3e-a894-f3effca05b9b" :answer/id #uuid "3c97f35c-4480-5e3e-a894-f3effca05b9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-375f59e1-b6c5-51a0-ad58-23511b54c59d" :answer/id #uuid "375f59e1-b6c5-51a0-ad58-23511b54c59d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc31709a-e3d1-56b4-9a97-dea545336cc4" :answer/id #uuid "cc31709a-e3d1-56b4-9a97-dea545336cc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5959bb5d-4929-5707-80e3-51ab7b1c379f" :answer/id #uuid "5959bb5d-4929-5707-80e3-51ab7b1c379f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f9115f7-c967-552e-babd-64a7c492372a" :answer/id #uuid "2f9115f7-c967-552e-babd-64a7c492372a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-f27f406f-a65a-51e2-a105-2cd7314e1515" :activity/id #uuid "f27f406f-a65a-51e2-a105-2cd7314e1515" :activity/title "The Jacobian" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048219 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-a74bfad6-ea65-5feb-a899-c8d57f2b8048" "step-7925d591-5b75-52ac-b9d8-3ec5418695ea" "step-304d533c-c6df-5eb2-8572-8dad82b0c2ff" "step-c634b432-1616-5094-a080-a0dd00d9d507" "step-5752fbe6-2298-595f-8f5f-87a185f8bc29"] :activity/first-step "step-a74bfad6-ea65-5feb-a899-c8d57f2b8048" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-a74bfad6-ea65-5feb-a899-c8d57f2b8048" :step/id #uuid "a74bfad6-ea65-5feb-a899-c8d57f2b8048" :step/content "question-abc95782-56f0-5602-a797-77bbd8bc8d07" :step/next "step-7925d591-5b75-52ac-b9d8-3ec5418695ea" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7925d591-5b75-52ac-b9d8-3ec5418695ea" :step/id #uuid "7925d591-5b75-52ac-b9d8-3ec5418695ea" :step/content 17592186278291 :step/next "step-304d533c-c6df-5eb2-8572-8dad82b0c2ff" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-304d533c-c6df-5eb2-8572-8dad82b0c2ff" :step/id #uuid "304d533c-c6df-5eb2-8572-8dad82b0c2ff" :step/content 17592186129527 :step/next "step-c634b432-1616-5094-a080-a0dd00d9d507" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c634b432-1616-5094-a080-a0dd00d9d507" :step/id #uuid "c634b432-1616-5094-a080-a0dd00d9d507" :step/content 17592186389195 :step/next "step-5752fbe6-2298-595f-8f5f-87a185f8bc29" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5752fbe6-2298-595f-8f5f-87a185f8bc29" :step/id #uuid "5752fbe6-2298-595f-8f5f-87a185f8bc29" :step/content 17592186281354 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129309 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-27f65119-9cfd-5858-830b-dc487011110a" "question-5fe451b2-edf1-59c7-ba6b-aec83b3dbee5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-27f65119-9cfd-5858-830b-dc487011110a" :question/id #uuid "27f65119-9cfd-5858-830b-dc487011110a" :question/math-academy-id "q-69345" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{5}{8}\\times 3-(8-10)^{-3}.$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, we compute the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{8}\\times 3-(8-10)^{-3}=\\frac{5}{8}\\times 3-(-2)^{-3}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that $(-2)^{-3}=\\frac{1}{(-2)^{3}}=-\\frac{1}{8}.$ So, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{8}\\times 3-(-2)^{-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{8}\\times 3-(-\\frac{1}{8}) & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{8}\\times \\frac{3}{1}+\\frac{1}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{5\\times 3}{8\\times 1}+\\frac{1}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{15}{8}+\\frac{1}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{15+1}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{16}{8} & = \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7a5fd354-5df8-5dcc-bf17-82ac638ded50"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7a5fd354-5df8-5dcc-bf17-82ac638ded50" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a5fd354-5df8-5dcc-bf17-82ac638ded50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b71f29a1-8d1a-5479-ac04-69c1694fac07" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c44f6e25-54af-5112-a2ff-488411a644f3" "answer-545f6b34-8b08-5486-9f0e-2cc84dac10e4" "answer-5923c943-f43e-5441-819c-fc4c38287552" "answer-b71f29a1-8d1a-5479-ac04-69c1694fac07" "answer-7575186d-b230-5c3f-951f-24397f6e911d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c44f6e25-54af-5112-a2ff-488411a644f3" :answer/id #uuid "c44f6e25-54af-5112-a2ff-488411a644f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-545f6b34-8b08-5486-9f0e-2cc84dac10e4" :answer/id #uuid "545f6b34-8b08-5486-9f0e-2cc84dac10e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5923c943-f43e-5441-819c-fc4c38287552" :answer/id #uuid "5923c943-f43e-5441-819c-fc4c38287552" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b71f29a1-8d1a-5479-ac04-69c1694fac07" :answer/id #uuid "b71f29a1-8d1a-5479-ac04-69c1694fac07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7575186d-b230-5c3f-951f-24397f6e911d" :answer/id #uuid "7575186d-b230-5c3f-951f-24397f6e911d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129310 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-355c3927-42d5-52b6-8af5-1388530c1ab2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-355c3927-42d5-52b6-8af5-1388530c1ab2" :question/id #uuid "355c3927-42d5-52b6-8af5-1388530c1ab2" :question/math-academy-id "q-171378" :question/problem "$(-1+7.35)^{0}\\times {5}^{-3}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, we compute the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n(-1+7.35)^{0}\\times {5}^{-3}=(6.35)^{0}\\times {5}^{-3}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that $(6.35)^{0}=1.$ So, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6.35)^{0}\\times {5}^{-3} & = \\\\ 1\\times {5}^{-3} & = \\\\ {5}^{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{5}^{-3}=\\frac{1}{{5}^{3}}=\\frac{1}{125}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3292a063-82f7-566f-97f5-25f4fc63cbef"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3292a063-82f7-566f-97f5-25f4fc63cbef" :answer-field/id #uuid "3292a063-82f7-566f-97f5-25f4fc63cbef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-90c61a4c-acb5-5943-83c3-2a9169499652" :answer-field/choices ["answer-90c61a4c-acb5-5943-83c3-2a9169499652"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90c61a4c-acb5-5943-83c3-2a9169499652" :answer/id #uuid "90c61a4c-acb5-5943-83c3-2a9169499652" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{125}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5fe451b2-edf1-59c7-ba6b-aec83b3dbee5" :question/id #uuid "5fe451b2-edf1-59c7-ba6b-aec83b3dbee5" :question/math-academy-id "q-175956" :question/problem "${2}^{-3}\\times (\\frac{8}{5}+4)=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nNotice that ${2}^{-3}=\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}.$ So, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{-3}\\times (\\frac{8}{5}+4) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}\\times (\\frac{8}{5}+4) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}\\times (\\frac{8}{5}+4) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}\\times \\frac{8+20}{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}\\times \\frac{28}{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{1\\times 28}{8\\times 5} & = \\\\ \\frac{1\\times 4\\times 7}{2\\times 4\\times 5} & = \\\\ \\frac{1\\times \\cancel{4}\\times 7}{2\\times \\cancel{4}\\times 5} & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-370651de-97e9-5350-9a2a-8b5e0ff4246c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-370651de-97e9-5350-9a2a-8b5e0ff4246c" :answer-field/id #uuid "370651de-97e9-5350-9a2a-8b5e0ff4246c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7a76c1ed-9c9a-5884-8b85-3040e0c60944" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7a76c1ed-9c9a-5884-8b85-3040e0c60944"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a76c1ed-9c9a-5884-8b85-3040e0c60944" :answer/id #uuid "7a76c1ed-9c9a-5884-8b85-3040e0c60944" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-dbf71e83-e6c5-5f76-a850-bb5e63425c3e" :activity/id #uuid "dbf71e83-e6c5-5f76-a850-bb5e63425c3e" :activity/title "Evaluating Expressions With Integer Exponents" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048599 :activity/course 17592186046648 :activity/steps ["step-128dae23-270e-52bb-9758-c300a092867a" "step-95845e10-8b08-5a84-8f24-4769592ec34a" "step-2c54203f-3a25-554b-95d3-3f146fa16ddb"] :activity/first-step "step-128dae23-270e-52bb-9758-c300a092867a" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-128dae23-270e-52bb-9758-c300a092867a" :step/id #uuid "128dae23-270e-52bb-9758-c300a092867a" :step/content "question-27f65119-9cfd-5858-830b-dc487011110a" :step/next "step-95845e10-8b08-5a84-8f24-4769592ec34a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-95845e10-8b08-5a84-8f24-4769592ec34a" :step/id #uuid "95845e10-8b08-5a84-8f24-4769592ec34a" :step/content "question-355c3927-42d5-52b6-8af5-1388530c1ab2" :step/next "step-2c54203f-3a25-554b-95d3-3f146fa16ddb" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2c54203f-3a25-554b-95d3-3f146fa16ddb" :step/id #uuid "2c54203f-3a25-554b-95d3-3f146fa16ddb" :step/content "question-5fe451b2-edf1-59c7-ba6b-aec83b3dbee5" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186180185 :question/answer-fields 17592186178654] [:db/retract 17592186179404 :answer-field/choices 17592186179408] [:db/retract 17592186179404 :answer-field/choices 17592186179409] [:db/retract 17592186179404 :answer-field/choices 17592186179405] [:db/retract 17592186179404 :answer-field/choices 17592186179406] [:db/retract 17592186179404 :answer-field/choices 17592186179407] {:db/id 17592186179688 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6d8b3a40-13c2-5419-a866-6118c0d389c8" "question-fe02f258-a8c1-593e-bacb-46d349ae065b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179690 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-19772385-86fe-59c3-9b8a-1626c506e897" "question-5cb7d692-f924-57ab-bd09-dd8cc202af02"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6d8b3a40-13c2-5419-a866-6118c0d389c8" :question/id #uuid "6d8b3a40-13c2-5419-a866-6118c0d389c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-131244" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2}F)$ for the vector field $F$ where\n\n$$\nF={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)\\,i+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)\\,j-x{z}^{4}\\,k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2}F)=\\frac{3}{2}∇\\cdot F.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y))+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y))+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-x{z}^{4}) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)-4x{z}^{3} \\\\  & =4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)-4x{z}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2}F) & =\\frac{3}{2}∇\\cdot F \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)-4x{z}^{3}) \\\\  & =6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)-6x{z}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-560133ea-a7b0-52cc-a804-28ad1422872c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-560133ea-a7b0-52cc-a804-28ad1422872c" :answer-field/id #uuid "560133ea-a7b0-52cc-a804-28ad1422872c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9da03a85-026e-5343-ae06-7ceb351c6a72" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a9b21b82-aeaf-5a49-88a9-1e22866dcd38" "answer-9b53fb88-54d3-5084-89ac-28e6c71dd00e" "answer-9da03a85-026e-5343-ae06-7ceb351c6a72" "answer-279dea5a-f4d5-586b-a072-0c9f9d03bc89" "answer-760b5f11-f68e-56f1-afde-6e7843ea5c43"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9b21b82-aeaf-5a49-88a9-1e22866dcd38" :answer/id #uuid "a9b21b82-aeaf-5a49-88a9-1e22866dcd38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2x{z}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b53fb88-54d3-5084-89ac-28e6c71dd00e" :answer/id #uuid "9b53fb88-54d3-5084-89ac-28e6c71dd00e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-x{z}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9da03a85-026e-5343-ae06-7ceb351c6a72" :answer/id #uuid "9da03a85-026e-5343-ae06-7ceb351c6a72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)-6x{z}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-279dea5a-f4d5-586b-a072-0c9f9d03bc89" :answer/id #uuid "279dea5a-f4d5-586b-a072-0c9f9d03bc89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)+xz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-760b5f11-f68e-56f1-afde-6e7843ea5c43" :answer/id #uuid "760b5f11-f68e-56f1-afde-6e7843ea5c43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-{z}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fe02f258-a8c1-593e-bacb-46d349ae065b" :question/id #uuid "fe02f258-a8c1-593e-bacb-46d349ae065b" :question/math-academy-id "q-105634" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\cdot (-3F)$ for the vector field $F$ where\n\n$$\nF=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,i+2xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,j-4z\\,k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (-3F) & =-3∇\\cdot F.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4z) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4 \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (-3F) & =-3∇\\cdot F \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2) \\\\  & =6(2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e04136be-f727-5add-9a25-13584d652f7a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e04136be-f727-5add-9a25-13584d652f7a" :answer-field/id #uuid "e04136be-f727-5add-9a25-13584d652f7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c917523d-92c4-54de-b0df-a6bf816b85b4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d31bc03e-05c6-5840-8321-3067c96b1d32" "answer-6e2395f7-fab5-51f4-8be4-159b63c3d4e8" "answer-22d2669f-748a-5d3e-add4-044dc27f9818" "answer-e786bbf5-86e3-5cad-83cf-c31ac0c9a27b" "answer-c917523d-92c4-54de-b0df-a6bf816b85b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d31bc03e-05c6-5840-8321-3067c96b1d32" :answer/id #uuid "d31bc03e-05c6-5840-8321-3067c96b1d32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3(2-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e2395f7-fab5-51f4-8be4-159b63c3d4e8" :answer/id #uuid "6e2395f7-fab5-51f4-8be4-159b63c3d4e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22d2669f-748a-5d3e-add4-044dc27f9818" :answer/id #uuid "22d2669f-748a-5d3e-add4-044dc27f9818" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6(2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e786bbf5-86e3-5cad-83cf-c31ac0c9a27b" :answer/id #uuid "e786bbf5-86e3-5cad-83cf-c31ac0c9a27b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6(2+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c917523d-92c4-54de-b0df-a6bf816b85b4" :answer/id #uuid "c917523d-92c4-54de-b0df-a6bf816b85b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6(2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180310 :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y)=⟨x,{x}^{2}y⟩$ and $f(x,y)=xy,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨y,x⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y)=1+{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =xy(1+{x}^{2})+⟨x,{x}^{2}y⟩\\cdot ⟨y,x⟩ \\\\  & =xy+{x}^{3}y+xy+{x}^{3}y \\\\  & =2xy+2{x}^{3}y \\\\  & =2xy(1+{x}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179404 :answer-field/correct "answer-3b9781e6-d514-50c9-8bc5-ef65fd44af25" :answer-field/choices ["answer-727ac25f-a90a-5dcd-bcbf-04adfe3d45f3" "answer-2d2f2f0d-40d7-5f2d-83f1-2ea1f486329b" "answer-3b9781e6-d514-50c9-8bc5-ef65fd44af25" "answer-1fbac9b0-3131-5b68-8747-b8662452e7bd" "answer-cc634756-be7d-5a9e-b487-b504317b94d7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-727ac25f-a90a-5dcd-bcbf-04adfe3d45f3" :answer/id #uuid "727ac25f-a90a-5dcd-bcbf-04adfe3d45f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2xy(1+x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d2f2f0d-40d7-5f2d-83f1-2ea1f486329b" :answer/id #uuid "2d2f2f0d-40d7-5f2d-83f1-2ea1f486329b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2xy(1+xy)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b9781e6-d514-50c9-8bc5-ef65fd44af25" :answer/id #uuid "3b9781e6-d514-50c9-8bc5-ef65fd44af25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2xy(1+{x}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fbac9b0-3131-5b68-8747-b8662452e7bd" :answer/id #uuid "1fbac9b0-3131-5b68-8747-b8662452e7bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2xy(1+{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc634756-be7d-5a9e-b487-b504317b94d7" :answer/id #uuid "cc634756-be7d-5a9e-b487-b504317b94d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2xy(1+{y}^{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-19772385-86fe-59c3-9b8a-1626c506e897" :question/id #uuid "19772385-86fe-59c3-9b8a-1626c506e897" :question/math-academy-id "q-105656" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y,z)=⟨xy,zy,zx⟩$ and $f(x,y,z)=xyz,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨yz,xz,xy⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(zy)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(zx)=y+z+x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =xyz(x+y+z)+⟨xy,zy,zx⟩\\cdot ⟨yz,xz,xy⟩ \\\\  & =xyz(x+y+z)+x{y}^{2}z+xy{z}^{2}+{x}^{2}yz \\\\  & =xyz(x+y+z)+xyz(x+y+z) \\\\  & =2xyz(x+y+z).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7f30e86d-bd3c-561f-bb1d-7773101df310"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7f30e86d-bd3c-561f-bb1d-7773101df310" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f30e86d-bd3c-561f-bb1d-7773101df310" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e167ec05-7ba8-54ee-88eb-33b8c7129f98" :answer-field/choices ["answer-48f71578-9dc8-5af1-8c23-0a20717bf08c" "answer-e167ec05-7ba8-54ee-88eb-33b8c7129f98" "answer-fe3a0413-baf6-5112-9242-7dcd5ce3749b" "answer-f9dde9b5-7512-5c76-9578-51e87312e497" "answer-2c8e7f9a-6d64-5d22-b5bc-95c71fed9a4b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48f71578-9dc8-5af1-8c23-0a20717bf08c" :answer/id #uuid "48f71578-9dc8-5af1-8c23-0a20717bf08c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2xyz(x+2y+z)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e167ec05-7ba8-54ee-88eb-33b8c7129f98" :answer/id #uuid "e167ec05-7ba8-54ee-88eb-33b8c7129f98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2xyz(x+y+z)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe3a0413-baf6-5112-9242-7dcd5ce3749b" :answer/id #uuid "fe3a0413-baf6-5112-9242-7dcd5ce3749b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xyz(2x+y+2z)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9dde9b5-7512-5c76-9578-51e87312e497" :answer/id #uuid "f9dde9b5-7512-5c76-9578-51e87312e497" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xyz(x+2y+3z)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c8e7f9a-6d64-5d22-b5bc-95c71fed9a4b" :answer/id #uuid "2c8e7f9a-6d64-5d22-b5bc-95c71fed9a4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xyz(x+y+2z)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5cb7d692-f924-57ab-bd09-dd8cc202af02" :question/id #uuid "5cb7d692-f924-57ab-bd09-dd8cc202af02" :question/math-academy-id "q-131289" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y,z)=⟨{y}^{2}z,{x}^{2}+z,{x}^{2}⟩$ and $f(x,y,z)=x+y-z,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨1,1,-1⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}z)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2})=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =(x+y-z)\\cdot 0+⟨{y}^{2}z,{x}^{2}+z,{x}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =0+{y}^{2}z+{x}^{2}+z-{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}^{2}z+z \\\\  & =z({y}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-402aba4f-11b8-5925-805f-969b29ff490f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-402aba4f-11b8-5925-805f-969b29ff490f" :answer-field/id #uuid "402aba4f-11b8-5925-805f-969b29ff490f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-18fc1a57-09dc-5787-b3e4-8f5ef0b7fc76" :answer-field/choices ["answer-48181509-820b-5e87-ba28-4511cc6dfe9f" "answer-5dbc2503-13f3-56f1-9ffe-484d847562c2" "answer-0e083018-a5e8-5516-b3a3-9c427afd469f" "answer-18fc1a57-09dc-5787-b3e4-8f5ef0b7fc76" "answer-53ef7803-126c-5a6e-93c7-7cf843ded9a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48181509-820b-5e87-ba28-4511cc6dfe9f" :answer/id #uuid "48181509-820b-5e87-ba28-4511cc6dfe9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z(x{y}^{2}+z)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5dbc2503-13f3-56f1-9ffe-484d847562c2" :answer/id #uuid "5dbc2503-13f3-56f1-9ffe-484d847562c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z(x{y}^{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e083018-a5e8-5516-b3a3-9c427afd469f" :answer/id #uuid "0e083018-a5e8-5516-b3a3-9c427afd469f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z(y+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18fc1a57-09dc-5787-b3e4-8f5ef0b7fc76" :answer/id #uuid "18fc1a57-09dc-5787-b3e4-8f5ef0b7fc76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z({y}^{2}+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53ef7803-126c-5a6e-93c7-7cf843ded9a0" :answer/id #uuid "53ef7803-126c-5a6e-93c7-7cf843ded9a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z({y}^{2}+x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180709 :tutorial/content "Recall that for functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ the product rule for differentiation is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d }{\\textrm d x}(f\\cdot g) = f\\dfrac{\\textrm d }{\\textrm d x}(g) +  g\\dfrac{\\textrm d }{\\textrm d x}(f).\n$$\n\nThere is an analogous rule for computing the divergence of the product of a vector field and a scalar field.\n\nSuppose that $\\mathbf F$ is a vector field and $f$ is a scalar field. Then, we have the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla \\cdot (f\\,\\mathbf F) = f\\, \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf {F}+  \\mathbf F \\cdot \\nabla \\! f\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere $\\nabla f$ is the gradient of $f.$\n\nNotice that the del operator $\\nabla$ acts on the terms in the same way as the $\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}$ operator in the product rule for differentiation!\n\nThere are a few other tips that we can use to remember this rule:\n\n- The term $\\nabla \\cdot (f\\,\\mathbf F)$ on the left-hand side must be a scalar field because it's a divergence. So, the two terms on the right-hand side must be scalar fields, too.\n\n- The term $f\\, \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf {F}$ on the right-hand side is a scalar field because both $f$ and $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F$ are scalar fields, and the product of two scalar fields is a scalar field. Note that this \"product\" is just regular multiplication.\n\n- The term $\\mathbf F \\cdot \\nabla \\! f$ on the right-hand side is a scalar field because both $\\mathbf F$ and $\\nabla f$ are *vector* fields, and the *dot product* of two vector fields is a scalar field." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179855 :activity/expected-seconds 600.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064233 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c9bc34bd-c944-573e-9a8a-bd4bb9a0f491" "question-a62d676a-9c38-5dd1-a066-72e04e4e8a97"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c9bc34bd-c944-573e-9a8a-bd4bb9a0f491" :question/id #uuid "c9bc34bd-c944-573e-9a8a-bd4bb9a0f491" :question/math-academy-id "q-31551" :question/problem "${(3+2{w}^{3})}^{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{2}={a}^{2}+2ab+{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=3$ and $b=2{w}^{3},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+2{w}^{3})^{2} & = \\\\ {3}^{2}+2(3)(2{w}^{3})+(2{w}^{3})^{2} & = \\\\ 9+12{w}^{3}+4{w}^{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c012204b-f827-5e31-922c-3c631ad51cc6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c012204b-f827-5e31-922c-3c631ad51cc6" :answer-field/id #uuid "c012204b-f827-5e31-922c-3c631ad51cc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-46ec2942-f6fe-5960-a870-5c13e581e7b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6598702c-b178-5390-8d47-dc145c750494" "answer-30e198a1-9cd9-532e-b734-b7de40702f8f" "answer-46ec2942-f6fe-5960-a870-5c13e581e7b0" "answer-b72d3e86-d7b2-5212-a462-13f5e6b36f94" "answer-2d91b24d-4cf0-5621-b56a-13fa12f96cc0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6598702c-b178-5390-8d47-dc145c750494" :answer/id #uuid "6598702c-b178-5390-8d47-dc145c750494" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9+12{w}^{3}+2{w}^{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30e198a1-9cd9-532e-b734-b7de40702f8f" :answer/id #uuid "30e198a1-9cd9-532e-b734-b7de40702f8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9+12{w}^{3}+2{w}^{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46ec2942-f6fe-5960-a870-5c13e581e7b0" :answer/id #uuid "46ec2942-f6fe-5960-a870-5c13e581e7b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9+12{w}^{3}+4{w}^{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b72d3e86-d7b2-5212-a462-13f5e6b36f94" :answer/id #uuid "b72d3e86-d7b2-5212-a462-13f5e6b36f94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9+4{w}^{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d91b24d-4cf0-5621-b56a-13fa12f96cc0" :answer/id #uuid "2d91b24d-4cf0-5621-b56a-13fa12f96cc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9+6{w}^{3}+2{w}^{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a62d676a-9c38-5dd1-a066-72e04e4e8a97" :question/id #uuid "a62d676a-9c38-5dd1-a066-72e04e4e8a97" :question/math-academy-id "q-33095" :question/problem "${(\\frac{1}{3}+{x}^{2})}^{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{2}={a}^{2}+2ab+{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=\\frac{1}{3}$ and $b={x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{1}{3}+{x}^{2})}^{2} & = \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+2(\\frac{1}{3})({x}^{2})+{({x}^{2})}^{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{2}+{x}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1248bc9c-da8e-5444-ae7b-ffd4127ab86f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1248bc9c-da8e-5444-ae7b-ffd4127ab86f" :answer-field/id #uuid "1248bc9c-da8e-5444-ae7b-ffd4127ab86f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-84c7c962-da54-5750-9444-176e8e186f3b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-174ed3f2-66bc-5124-aa00-570861734082" "answer-f2c7773c-a23f-5f60-a9f6-ea4c2e71ce2b" "answer-84c7c962-da54-5750-9444-176e8e186f3b" "answer-0d65759d-e36d-5045-acc5-db2984da989f" "answer-ea56582c-7d40-5467-bb1c-047ef74db56a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-174ed3f2-66bc-5124-aa00-570861734082" :answer/id #uuid "174ed3f2-66bc-5124-aa00-570861734082" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2c7773c-a23f-5f60-a9f6-ea4c2e71ce2b" :answer/id #uuid "f2c7773c-a23f-5f60-a9f6-ea4c2e71ce2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84c7c962-da54-5750-9444-176e8e186f3b" :answer/id #uuid "84c7c962-da54-5750-9444-176e8e186f3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{2}+{x}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d65759d-e36d-5045-acc5-db2984da989f" :answer/id #uuid "0d65759d-e36d-5045-acc5-db2984da989f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}+{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea56582c-7d40-5467-bb1c-047ef74db56a" :answer/id #uuid "ea56582c-7d40-5467-bb1c-047ef74db56a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}+{x}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064234 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2be683e9-4308-5a65-9d13-a50367058c8f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2be683e9-4308-5a65-9d13-a50367058c8f" :question/id #uuid "2be683e9-4308-5a65-9d13-a50367058c8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-33114" :question/problem "${(2a-{b}^{2})}^{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n(x-y)^{2}={x}^{2}-2xy+{y}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2a$ and $y={b}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(2a-{b}^{2})}^{2} & = \\\\ (2a)^{2}-2(2a)({b}^{2})+{({b}^{2})}^{2} & = \\\\ 4{a}^{2}-4a{b}^{2}+{b}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ec200471-10b2-5681-96c2-657a58983bc0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ec200471-10b2-5681-96c2-657a58983bc0" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec200471-10b2-5681-96c2-657a58983bc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-68f6dbdb-d583-5244-98af-d51948d327ee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f2c12960-665c-559d-b833-9b56dd740b5f" "answer-d24981a6-c6ea-5260-94b3-3a43009f92cd" "answer-823a99ee-ed71-595d-979e-7d9efe2268fa" "answer-68f6dbdb-d583-5244-98af-d51948d327ee" "answer-8ebe3a75-ff92-5c14-947a-6c9b06c84f8c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2c12960-665c-559d-b833-9b56dd740b5f" :answer/id #uuid "f2c12960-665c-559d-b833-9b56dd740b5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{a}^{2}+4a{b}^{2}+{b}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d24981a6-c6ea-5260-94b3-3a43009f92cd" :answer/id #uuid "d24981a6-c6ea-5260-94b3-3a43009f92cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{a}^{2}-2a{b}^{2}-{b}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-823a99ee-ed71-595d-979e-7d9efe2268fa" :answer/id #uuid "823a99ee-ed71-595d-979e-7d9efe2268fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{a}^{2}+{b}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68f6dbdb-d583-5244-98af-d51948d327ee" :answer/id #uuid "68f6dbdb-d583-5244-98af-d51948d327ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{a}^{2}-4a{b}^{2}+{b}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ebe3a75-ff92-5c14-947a-6c9b06c84f8c" :answer/id #uuid "8ebe3a75-ff92-5c14-947a-6c9b06c84f8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{a}^{2}-{b}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-2067b6ed-7ec5-593e-ba9b-4ee8e220676e" :activity/id #uuid "2067b6ed-7ec5-593e-ba9b-4ee8e220676e" :activity/title "Squaring Binomials" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049847 :activity/course 17592186046648 :activity/steps ["step-b9dd9bf4-659c-5cef-a140-f5ba0f516f13" "step-1a9645f9-f395-5430-af2e-ac99c6e17870" "step-4146d3be-051f-5fcc-ae2f-3ac52db899e7"] :activity/first-step "step-b9dd9bf4-659c-5cef-a140-f5ba0f516f13" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-b9dd9bf4-659c-5cef-a140-f5ba0f516f13" :step/id #uuid "b9dd9bf4-659c-5cef-a140-f5ba0f516f13" :step/content "question-c9bc34bd-c944-573e-9a8a-bd4bb9a0f491" :step/next "step-1a9645f9-f395-5430-af2e-ac99c6e17870" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1a9645f9-f395-5430-af2e-ac99c6e17870" :step/id #uuid "1a9645f9-f395-5430-af2e-ac99c6e17870" :step/content "question-a62d676a-9c38-5dd1-a066-72e04e4e8a97" :step/next "step-4146d3be-051f-5fcc-ae2f-3ac52db899e7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4146d3be-051f-5fcc-ae2f-3ac52db899e7" :step/id #uuid "4146d3be-051f-5fcc-ae2f-3ac52db899e7" :step/content "question-2be683e9-4308-5a65-9d13-a50367058c8f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073881 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bad4ad2c-65e9-50c0-a0af-a1c173627efa" "question-bdac105a-b535-5e32-bc94-795efb94b947"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073563 :question/problem "Adam has a cedar tree and willow tree in his garden. The ratio of the height of the cedar tree to the height of a willow tree is $8:5.$ If the height of the cedar tree is $24$ meters, what is the height of the willow tree?" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio ${\\color{blue}8}:{\\color{red}5}$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}8}}{{\\color{red}5}}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the height of the   cedar tree and the denominator represents the height of the  willow tree.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $24$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}8}\\times 3}{{\\color{red}5}\\times 3} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}24}}{{\\color{red}15}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if the height of the cedar tree is $24$ meters, the height of the willow tree is $15$ meters." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073882 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-34bd5498-60c5-56d4-9f94-63016d557040" "question-4cce5310-2253-544b-a45b-5b307f4192ed"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073564 :question/problem "The ratio of sand to crushed stone in concrete is $\\dfrac{3}{2}.$ If Daniel has $80$ kilograms of crushed stone available to make concrete, what amount of sand should he use?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of sand to crushed stone in concrete is $\\dfrac{3}{2}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the amount of sand and the denominator represents the amount of crushed stone.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $80$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $40\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}3}\\times 40}{{\\color{red}2}\\times 40} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}120}}{{\\color{red}80}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $80$ kilograms of crushed stone, Daniel must use $120$ kilograms of sand." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-bad4ad2c-65e9-50c0-a0af-a1c173627efa" :question/id #uuid "bad4ad2c-65e9-50c0-a0af-a1c173627efa" :question/math-academy-id "q-60149" :question/problem "There are $60$ peaches in Sophia's store. The ratio of peaches to pears is $6:5.$ How many pears are there in Sophia's store?" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio $6:5$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of peaches and the denominator represents the number of pears.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $60$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6\\times 10}{5\\times 10}=\\frac{60}{50}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $50$ pears in Sophia's store." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1247e2dc-2998-585b-8060-dacb4eae3f3f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1247e2dc-2998-585b-8060-dacb4eae3f3f" :answer-field/id #uuid "1247e2dc-2998-585b-8060-dacb4eae3f3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3d34d00c-fa58-5181-af8a-14174d80eefd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-33f4d7f9-6ff2-568a-9031-8fd2bd5573e5" "answer-57c8725d-c196-52c3-b69d-90a08cc21396" "answer-5e646964-d2b1-5506-ab26-40f144105c1a" "answer-8f77cbd4-c41a-5a41-91f6-297781ff2b82" "answer-3d34d00c-fa58-5181-af8a-14174d80eefd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33f4d7f9-6ff2-568a-9031-8fd2bd5573e5" :answer/id #uuid "33f4d7f9-6ff2-568a-9031-8fd2bd5573e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57c8725d-c196-52c3-b69d-90a08cc21396" :answer/id #uuid "57c8725d-c196-52c3-b69d-90a08cc21396" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e646964-d2b1-5506-ab26-40f144105c1a" :answer/id #uuid "5e646964-d2b1-5506-ab26-40f144105c1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f77cbd4-c41a-5a41-91f6-297781ff2b82" :answer/id #uuid "8f77cbd4-c41a-5a41-91f6-297781ff2b82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d34d00c-fa58-5181-af8a-14174d80eefd" :answer/id #uuid "3d34d00c-fa58-5181-af8a-14174d80eefd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bdac105a-b535-5e32-bc94-795efb94b947" :question/id #uuid "bdac105a-b535-5e32-bc94-795efb94b947" :question/math-academy-id "q-60307" :question/problem "To prepare a homemade nasal spray, the ratio of salt (in grams) to cups of water is $\\frac{5}{2}.$ If Eliza wants to make a nasal spray with $15$ grams of salt, how many cups of water should she use?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of salt (in grams) to cups of water is $\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the amount of salt and the denominator represents the number of cups of water.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $15$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 3}{2\\times 3}=\\frac{15}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $15$ grams of salt, Eliza must use $6$ cups of water." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2eb1723d-2257-5fd9-9e08-adc5fefc137a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2eb1723d-2257-5fd9-9e08-adc5fefc137a" :answer-field/id #uuid "2eb1723d-2257-5fd9-9e08-adc5fefc137a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6954abd4-3414-55e5-a56a-f7af8cf2d213" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0eb7bebc-75f0-5757-9e6a-5d7b9908d477" "answer-66bcfbbc-d270-5b34-81b6-d9415ac2cfe0" "answer-6954abd4-3414-55e5-a56a-f7af8cf2d213" "answer-8db65988-4f85-5444-b7a4-a6e93cdb3f85" "answer-8c87e2d1-9905-55f6-9540-ada0f504eaf9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0eb7bebc-75f0-5757-9e6a-5d7b9908d477" :answer/id #uuid "0eb7bebc-75f0-5757-9e6a-5d7b9908d477" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66bcfbbc-d270-5b34-81b6-d9415ac2cfe0" :answer/id #uuid "66bcfbbc-d270-5b34-81b6-d9415ac2cfe0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6954abd4-3414-55e5-a56a-f7af8cf2d213" :answer/id #uuid "6954abd4-3414-55e5-a56a-f7af8cf2d213" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8db65988-4f85-5444-b7a4-a6e93cdb3f85" :answer/id #uuid "8db65988-4f85-5444-b7a4-a6e93cdb3f85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c87e2d1-9905-55f6-9540-ada0f504eaf9" :answer/id #uuid "8c87e2d1-9905-55f6-9540-ada0f504eaf9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-34bd5498-60c5-56d4-9f94-63016d557040" :question/id #uuid "34bd5498-60c5-56d4-9f94-63016d557040" :question/math-academy-id "q-147042" :question/problem "The ratio of T-shirts to pairs of jeans in David's closet is $\\frac{5}{2}.$ If David has $4$ pairs of jeans in his closet, how many T-shirts does David have?" :question/worked-solution "The ratio of T-shirts to pairs of jeans in David's closet is $\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of T-shirts and the denominator represents the number of pairs of jeans.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $4$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 2}{2\\times 2}=\\frac{10}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, David has $10$ T-shirts in his closet." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e5c43b1e-0107-5054-a334-26f92d083760"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e5c43b1e-0107-5054-a334-26f92d083760" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5c43b1e-0107-5054-a334-26f92d083760" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-42bac3d2-6074-51d7-a785-2d4d396435e5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-42bac3d2-6074-51d7-a785-2d4d396435e5" "answer-e4bf3b23-46d3-5e64-8a4c-1960f1e8f67f" "answer-c6023bed-d787-542d-b6c5-a662eeb68513" "answer-00ea9969-143b-5d82-8308-78472d749663" "answer-4ec82291-8ad2-5012-9943-f4982692d756"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42bac3d2-6074-51d7-a785-2d4d396435e5" :answer/id #uuid "42bac3d2-6074-51d7-a785-2d4d396435e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4bf3b23-46d3-5e64-8a4c-1960f1e8f67f" :answer/id #uuid "e4bf3b23-46d3-5e64-8a4c-1960f1e8f67f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6023bed-d787-542d-b6c5-a662eeb68513" :answer/id #uuid "c6023bed-d787-542d-b6c5-a662eeb68513" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00ea9969-143b-5d82-8308-78472d749663" :answer/id #uuid "00ea9969-143b-5d82-8308-78472d749663" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ec82291-8ad2-5012-9943-f4982692d756" :answer/id #uuid "4ec82291-8ad2-5012-9943-f4982692d756" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4cce5310-2253-544b-a45b-5b307f4192ed" :question/id #uuid "4cce5310-2253-544b-a45b-5b307f4192ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-147047" :question/problem "Sophie is baking a pie. The recipe for the pie dough states that the ratio of sugar to melted butter is $\\frac{3}{2}.$ If she decides to use $4$ cups of melted butter, how many cups of sugar does she need to use?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of sugar to melted butter is $\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of cups of sugar and the denominator represents the number of cups of melted butter.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $4$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 2}{2\\times 2}=\\frac{6}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $4$ cups of melted butter, Sophie must use $6$ cups of sugar." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f5233b41-f23f-5e4f-b8ad-e6c6136880ca"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f5233b41-f23f-5e4f-b8ad-e6c6136880ca" :answer-field/id #uuid "f5233b41-f23f-5e4f-b8ad-e6c6136880ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-16808e05-3101-5cfc-8fed-add05e727788" :answer-field/choices ["answer-56826d19-14f1-50b2-8905-418eb236e355" "answer-27e725b2-a1d9-58c5-885d-662a5b0457e0" "answer-49161eab-92bb-5d1b-8cdc-86af95320bb5" "answer-16808e05-3101-5cfc-8fed-add05e727788" "answer-1da45d8a-6a82-51be-b61b-765f9dfd5e36"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56826d19-14f1-50b2-8905-418eb236e355" :answer/id #uuid "56826d19-14f1-50b2-8905-418eb236e355" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27e725b2-a1d9-58c5-885d-662a5b0457e0" :answer/id #uuid "27e725b2-a1d9-58c5-885d-662a5b0457e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49161eab-92bb-5d1b-8cdc-86af95320bb5" :answer/id #uuid "49161eab-92bb-5d1b-8cdc-86af95320bb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16808e05-3101-5cfc-8fed-add05e727788" :answer/id #uuid "16808e05-3101-5cfc-8fed-add05e727788" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1da45d8a-6a82-51be-b61b-765f9dfd5e36" :answer/id #uuid "1da45d8a-6a82-51be-b61b-765f9dfd5e36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074967 :tutorial/content "Sometimes, we are given a ratio and want to find an amount. In these cases, it's helpful to use equivalent fractions. \n\nFor example, if the ratio of cows to sheep on Margaret's farm is $11:7$, and she has $22$ cows, how many sheep are there on the farm?\n\nTo solve this, we start with the ratio ${\\color{blue}11}:{\\color{red}7}$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}11}{\\color{red}7}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of cows and the denominator represents the number of sheep.\n\nSince there are $22$ cows on the farm, we would like a numerator of $22.$ We make this by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}11}\\times 2}{{\\color{red}7}\\times 2} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}22}}{{\\color{red}14}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is now the number of sheep on the farm if there are $22$ cows. Therefore, on Margaret's farm, there are $\\color{red}14$ sheep." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073981 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073740 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ddf5db22-7c12-5596-b4f6-5a61a8187c11" "question-1816745e-33d2-5605-bad0-d9ea4d6d5feb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ddf5db22-7c12-5596-b4f6-5a61a8187c11" :question/id #uuid "ddf5db22-7c12-5596-b4f6-5a61a8187c11" :question/math-academy-id "q-59828" :question/problem "If $10$ children ate $15$ cakes, what number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of eaten cakes to children is $3:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there are $3$ eaten cakes for every $\\boxed{}\\,$ children." :question/worked-solution "Since $10$ children can eat $15$ cakes, the ratio of cakes to children is $15:10.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,15 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,10 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,5 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,5 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,3 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThat means that $3:2$ is equivalent to $15:10.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of eaten cakes to children is $3:2\\,$ because there are $3$ cakes for every $2\\,$ children.\"\n\nThe missing number is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a7379773-3775-53b0-a3c8-4af0a853a08a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a7379773-3775-53b0-a3c8-4af0a853a08a" :answer-field/id #uuid "a7379773-3775-53b0-a3c8-4af0a853a08a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-311f524f-5dec-5e52-ac4c-9fb446367ae9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-640e11a1-45f1-5bd9-ba70-d2bd9afff6a5" "answer-6b8d1a24-f0b3-5957-bac1-4b551d6b4aff" "answer-311f524f-5dec-5e52-ac4c-9fb446367ae9" "answer-8790ecbf-d319-56cd-88f6-19ef7c84fee4" "answer-736365bf-c5ec-516a-96d3-5dcf4aad4bc0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-640e11a1-45f1-5bd9-ba70-d2bd9afff6a5" :answer/id #uuid "640e11a1-45f1-5bd9-ba70-d2bd9afff6a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b8d1a24-f0b3-5957-bac1-4b551d6b4aff" :answer/id #uuid "6b8d1a24-f0b3-5957-bac1-4b551d6b4aff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-311f524f-5dec-5e52-ac4c-9fb446367ae9" :answer/id #uuid "311f524f-5dec-5e52-ac4c-9fb446367ae9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8790ecbf-d319-56cd-88f6-19ef7c84fee4" :answer/id #uuid "8790ecbf-d319-56cd-88f6-19ef7c84fee4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-736365bf-c5ec-516a-96d3-5dcf4aad4bc0" :answer/id #uuid "736365bf-c5ec-516a-96d3-5dcf4aad4bc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1816745e-33d2-5605-bad0-d9ea4d6d5feb" :question/id #uuid "1816745e-33d2-5605-bad0-d9ea4d6d5feb" :question/math-academy-id "q-59896" :question/problem "![](images/e6/e6c5263a440942da90d5ed6dc6a87e9e6caa0848dfb23c1a904eb828dfcaaeb1.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of rectangles to pentagons is $1:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there is $1$ rectangle for every $\\boxed{}$ pentagons." :question/worked-solution "First, we count the number of rectangles. We see that there are $2$ rectangles.\n\nThen, we count the number of pentagons. We see that there are $2$ pentagons.\n\nSo the ratio of rectangles to pentagons is $2:2.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,1 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $1:1$ is equivalent to $2:2.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of rectangles to pentagons is $1:1$ because there is $1$ rectangle for every $1$ pentagon.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fa08328e-cc55-5205-a1b2-f02f8b69f734"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fa08328e-cc55-5205-a1b2-f02f8b69f734" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa08328e-cc55-5205-a1b2-f02f8b69f734" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cd10f7eb-7f59-5705-9648-668ef168f8d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd10f7eb-7f59-5705-9648-668ef168f8d4" "answer-2b8636ec-a6ca-5436-8dd7-6da7ca001b95" "answer-d3ee81e2-8914-5cd6-8aba-c7a5b8a811e5" "answer-b6f1e389-8ab5-503e-b205-cc5f0bcc7461" "answer-c459ed53-041f-5cf1-a8ab-49b000eb425c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd10f7eb-7f59-5705-9648-668ef168f8d4" :answer/id #uuid "cd10f7eb-7f59-5705-9648-668ef168f8d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b8636ec-a6ca-5436-8dd7-6da7ca001b95" :answer/id #uuid "2b8636ec-a6ca-5436-8dd7-6da7ca001b95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3ee81e2-8914-5cd6-8aba-c7a5b8a811e5" :answer/id #uuid "d3ee81e2-8914-5cd6-8aba-c7a5b8a811e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6f1e389-8ab5-503e-b205-cc5f0bcc7461" :answer/id #uuid "b6f1e389-8ab5-503e-b205-cc5f0bcc7461" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c459ed53-041f-5cf1-a8ab-49b000eb425c" :answer/id #uuid "c459ed53-041f-5cf1-a8ab-49b000eb425c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073739 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ec0c1b9c-5490-5482-a264-c0fe31855e42"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ec0c1b9c-5490-5482-a264-c0fe31855e42" :question/id #uuid "ec0c1b9c-5490-5482-a264-c0fe31855e42" :question/math-academy-id "q-101444" :question/problem "![](images/ed/eda2132e8e050399298b97dc9d36cf27862d6aa4625e7aa870bb4c8fd246e781.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of triangles to the number of pentagons?" :question/worked-solution "We count the number of triangles. We see that there are $2$ triangles.\n\nWe count the number of pentagons. We see that there are $4$ pentagons.\n\nSo the ratio of triangles to pentagons is $2:4.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers in a ratio by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,4 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of triangles to pentagons is $1:2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f2e569b9-68b5-54d0-bd0f-496bb3345979"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f2e569b9-68b5-54d0-bd0f-496bb3345979" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2e569b9-68b5-54d0-bd0f-496bb3345979" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a3480f70-f3e4-5b52-9b49-7446ba7d2f81" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a3480f70-f3e4-5b52-9b49-7446ba7d2f81" "answer-9a2c18ff-74f1-5d6b-965e-9c4142e35106" "answer-0ab0f3fb-4e36-5cb7-9b92-bf6665005eea" "answer-4b95827d-b1f3-513f-a04b-4e3930a7a8ff" "answer-c8575184-e89c-5e39-8b80-accc5525b223"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3480f70-f3e4-5b52-9b49-7446ba7d2f81" :answer/id #uuid "a3480f70-f3e4-5b52-9b49-7446ba7d2f81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1:2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a2c18ff-74f1-5d6b-965e-9c4142e35106" :answer/id #uuid "9a2c18ff-74f1-5d6b-965e-9c4142e35106" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1:4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ab0f3fb-4e36-5cb7-9b92-bf6665005eea" :answer/id #uuid "0ab0f3fb-4e36-5cb7-9b92-bf6665005eea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2:1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b95827d-b1f3-513f-a04b-4e3930a7a8ff" :answer/id #uuid "4b95827d-b1f3-513f-a04b-4e3930a7a8ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2:2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8575184-e89c-5e39-8b80-accc5525b223" :answer/id #uuid "c8575184-e89c-5e39-8b80-accc5525b223" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2:6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-34509cbd-152a-5cd3-b3bc-231dc0557f02" :activity/id #uuid "34509cbd-152a-5cd3-b3bc-231dc0557f02" :activity/title "Equivalent Ratios" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048508 :activity/course 17592186046648 :activity/steps ["step-2b306b5b-d4d0-5bd9-ad85-47853cadb9b4" "step-f85a5132-bc8d-5028-bf7c-c2b4e0758ecd" "step-338c847b-f4c7-5b56-ae4c-a5bc33c176b9"] :activity/first-step "step-2b306b5b-d4d0-5bd9-ad85-47853cadb9b4" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-2b306b5b-d4d0-5bd9-ad85-47853cadb9b4" :step/id #uuid "2b306b5b-d4d0-5bd9-ad85-47853cadb9b4" :step/content "question-ddf5db22-7c12-5596-b4f6-5a61a8187c11" :step/next "step-f85a5132-bc8d-5028-bf7c-c2b4e0758ecd" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f85a5132-bc8d-5028-bf7c-c2b4e0758ecd" :step/id #uuid "f85a5132-bc8d-5028-bf7c-c2b4e0758ecd" :step/content "question-1816745e-33d2-5605-bad0-d9ea4d6d5feb" :step/next "step-338c847b-f4c7-5b56-ae4c-a5bc33c176b9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-338c847b-f4c7-5b56-ae4c-a5bc33c176b9" :step/id #uuid "338c847b-f4c7-5b56-ae4c-a5bc33c176b9" :step/content "question-ec0c1b9c-5490-5482-a264-c0fe31855e42" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186244108 :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\lambda v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -8+k \\\\ 3 & 5k\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =2k[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}k-10 \\\\ -6+5k\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4k \\\\ 2k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}k-10=-4k, \\\\ -6+5k=2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $k$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nk-10=-4k\\,⟹\\,k=2.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $k=2$ into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6+5k & =2k \\\\ -6+5(2) & =2(2) \\\\ 4 & =4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a true statement.\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $k=2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119802 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a325c3ab-0a0f-53da-bbb5-9670c5e960cd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a325c3ab-0a0f-53da-bbb5-9670c5e960cd" :question/id #uuid "a325c3ab-0a0f-53da-bbb5-9670c5e960cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-34159" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find $2u+v.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply each component of $u$ by $2.$ Then, we add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2u+v & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2+3 \\\\ 6+1 \\\\ 4+4 \\\\ 8+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-11c37918-e510-58d2-94fc-f2b5cad62a09"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-11c37918-e510-58d2-94fc-f2b5cad62a09" :answer-field/id #uuid "11c37918-e510-58d2-94fc-f2b5cad62a09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e86c3aac-878d-529e-a568-e3a364649363" :answer-field/choices ["answer-99975d59-e39c-52da-aa07-1f7f91d44f57" "answer-e86c3aac-878d-529e-a568-e3a364649363" "answer-29e67aff-720a-5267-bf31-39e69fb8ece0" "answer-b3ff84af-5a99-5d13-ba4f-d0c92cc0f1ea" "answer-e5e52666-64b5-5697-9e5e-fcded35b39e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99975d59-e39c-52da-aa07-1f7f91d44f57" :answer/id #uuid "99975d59-e39c-52da-aa07-1f7f91d44f57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e86c3aac-878d-529e-a568-e3a364649363" :answer/id #uuid "e86c3aac-878d-529e-a568-e3a364649363" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29e67aff-720a-5267-bf31-39e69fb8ece0" :answer/id #uuid "29e67aff-720a-5267-bf31-39e69fb8ece0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3ff84af-5a99-5d13-ba4f-d0c92cc0f1ea" :answer/id #uuid "b3ff84af-5a99-5d13-ba4f-d0c92cc0f1ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e5e52666-64b5-5697-9e5e-fcded35b39e4" :answer/id #uuid "e5e52666-64b5-5697-9e5e-fcded35b39e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060142 :question/problem "Simplify the statement $¬(A⇒B).$" :question/worked-solution "The conditional statement $P⇒Q$ is logically equivalent to the disjunction $¬P∨Q:$\n\nSo, in this case, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$$\n¬(A⇒B)≡¬(¬A∨B)\n$$\n\nDistributing the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law, we have\n\n$$\n¬(¬A∨B)≡¬(¬A)∧¬B.\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negation, we reach\n\n$$\nA∧¬B.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $A∧¬B.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186057218 :answer-field/correct 17592186057220 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105826 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-510156d7-b5c0-5e8b-8cd5-32b7f7e0537d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-510156d7-b5c0-5e8b-8cd5-32b7f7e0537d" :question/id #uuid "510156d7-b5c0-5e8b-8cd5-32b7f7e0537d" :question/math-academy-id "q-331503" :question/problem "A fair coin is flipped $5$ times. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, what is the probability that the coin lands on heads at most $3$ times?\n\nRounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times the coin lands on heads.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- There are $n=5$ flips.\n\n- The probability of landing heads is $p=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(5,\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for the probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x}){(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x}{(1-\\frac{1}{2})}^{5-x} \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x}){(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{5-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that at most $3$ of the $5$ flips are heads. So, we compute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =P(X=0)+P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{0}){(\\frac{1}{2})}^{0}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{5}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{1}){(\\frac{1}{2})}^{1}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{4} \\\\  & \\,+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{2}){(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3}){(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =(1+5+10+10)\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{5} \\\\  & =26\\cdot \\frac{1}{32} \\\\  & =0.813,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b9607223-8ad8-5973-98c0-43e17bad1ef9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b9607223-8ad8-5973-98c0-43e17bad1ef9" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9607223-8ad8-5973-98c0-43e17bad1ef9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0b95860c-921b-57fb-b5ec-46baec795536" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0b95860c-921b-57fb-b5ec-46baec795536"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b95860c-921b-57fb-b5ec-46baec795536" :answer/id #uuid "0b95860c-921b-57fb-b5ec-46baec795536" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.813" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-6dbf44c1-0a17-5860-b722-2be7efe51fed" :activity/id #uuid "6dbf44c1-0a17-5860-b722-2be7efe51fed" :activity/title "Quiz 1" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-ff156b25-7c2a-51a2-a6c6-e705bb9dabd4" "step-a3893880-47b4-50e9-a392-f2cb742adf65" "step-5dd82d00-4234-54d2-a846-7b8eca37409b" "step-05a87747-f2bd-5213-af84-8786d8887033" "step-fb598ac6-3d8c-5d31-b145-37cec278adcc" "step-c20ee976-ed2a-5a9d-aba3-56657afe8c97"] :activity/first-step "step-ff156b25-7c2a-51a2-a6c6-e705bb9dabd4" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-ff156b25-7c2a-51a2-a6c6-e705bb9dabd4" :step/id #uuid "ff156b25-7c2a-51a2-a6c6-e705bb9dabd4" :step/content 17592186388355 :step/next "step-a3893880-47b4-50e9-a392-f2cb742adf65" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a3893880-47b4-50e9-a392-f2cb742adf65" :step/id #uuid "a3893880-47b4-50e9-a392-f2cb742adf65" :step/content 17592186244108 :step/next "step-5dd82d00-4234-54d2-a846-7b8eca37409b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5dd82d00-4234-54d2-a846-7b8eca37409b" :step/id #uuid "5dd82d00-4234-54d2-a846-7b8eca37409b" :step/content 17592186262922 :step/next "step-05a87747-f2bd-5213-af84-8786d8887033" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-05a87747-f2bd-5213-af84-8786d8887033" :step/id #uuid "05a87747-f2bd-5213-af84-8786d8887033" :step/content "question-a325c3ab-0a0f-53da-bbb5-9670c5e960cd" :step/next "step-fb598ac6-3d8c-5d31-b145-37cec278adcc" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fb598ac6-3d8c-5d31-b145-37cec278adcc" :step/id #uuid "fb598ac6-3d8c-5d31-b145-37cec278adcc" :step/content 17592186060142 :step/next "step-c20ee976-ed2a-5a9d-aba3-56657afe8c97" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c20ee976-ed2a-5a9d-aba3-56657afe8c97" :step/id #uuid "c20ee976-ed2a-5a9d-aba3-56657afe8c97" :step/content "question-510156d7-b5c0-5e8b-8cd5-32b7f7e0537d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064217 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9cfc88f5-5c61-5b90-beb5-64a3476a024f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9cfc88f5-5c61-5b90-beb5-64a3476a024f" :question/id #uuid "9cfc88f5-5c61-5b90-beb5-64a3476a024f" :question/math-academy-id "q-44727" :question/problem "$3x({x}^{2}y+2)=$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply each term inside the parentheses by the term outside the parentheses, simplify using the rules of exponents, and then we add the results together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x({x}^{2}y+2) & = \\\\ 3x({x}^{2}y)+3x(2) & = \\\\ 3\\cdot {x}^{2+1}y+6x & = \\\\ 3{x}^{3}y+6x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7d5fa659-d7d1-55a1-83c5-184b6ed1af7f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7d5fa659-d7d1-55a1-83c5-184b6ed1af7f" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d5fa659-d7d1-55a1-83c5-184b6ed1af7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f38cbb7a-75fa-5860-832a-bf4ea3489c86" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1383eea4-8385-5b80-a00d-bc4a381cec34" "answer-f4ba294a-378d-5da9-9fd9-e632d9345e57" "answer-80fd8b82-26bf-59a6-af6c-1efba9feb3e8" "answer-f38cbb7a-75fa-5860-832a-bf4ea3489c86" "answer-469c4db6-332e-52b7-9453-76a3e2e8733c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1383eea4-8385-5b80-a00d-bc4a381cec34" :answer/id #uuid "1383eea4-8385-5b80-a00d-bc4a381cec34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{3}+6x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4ba294a-378d-5da9-9fd9-e632d9345e57" :answer/id #uuid "f4ba294a-378d-5da9-9fd9-e632d9345e57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{3}y+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80fd8b82-26bf-59a6-af6c-1efba9feb3e8" :answer/id #uuid "80fd8b82-26bf-59a6-af6c-1efba9feb3e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{3}y+3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f38cbb7a-75fa-5860-832a-bf4ea3489c86" :answer/id #uuid "f38cbb7a-75fa-5860-832a-bf4ea3489c86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{3}y+6x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-469c4db6-332e-52b7-9453-76a3e2e8733c" :answer/id #uuid "469c4db6-332e-52b7-9453-76a3e2e8733c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{3}y+6xy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064215 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-aad55e06-4983-5ff1-b72a-41466f8cbb81"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-aad55e06-4983-5ff1-b72a-41466f8cbb81" :question/id #uuid "aad55e06-4983-5ff1-b72a-41466f8cbb81" :question/math-academy-id "q-110835" :question/problem "$-{a}^{2}(2{a}^{4}-3{a}^{2}-6)=$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply each term inside the parentheses by the term outside the parentheses, simplify using the rules of exponents, and then we add the results together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{a}^{2}(2{a}^{4}-3{a}^{2}-6) & = \\\\ (-{a}^{2})(2{a}^{4})+(-{a}^{2})(-3{a}^{2})+(-{a}^{2})(-6) & = \\\\ ((-1)\\cdot 2)({a}^{2}\\cdot {a}^{4})+((-1)\\cdot (-3))({a}^{2}\\cdot {a}^{2})+((-1)\\cdot (-6))({a}^{2}) & = \\\\ (-2){a}^{2+4}+(3){a}^{2+2}+(6){a}^{2} & = \\\\ -2{a}^{6}+3{a}^{4}+6{a}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f72b4150-b00a-5010-ad64-3981725c8bb1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f72b4150-b00a-5010-ad64-3981725c8bb1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f72b4150-b00a-5010-ad64-3981725c8bb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f80efb83-27d0-51e9-bdfb-27593f4de169" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4ff82ea5-a53e-581b-bf6e-70bfe7b8756b" "answer-4cfe73b4-b0e8-50ac-850e-f133bc075de3" "answer-f80efb83-27d0-51e9-bdfb-27593f4de169" "answer-47ed6dd6-b0d1-5887-8326-53ee4a3b117a" "answer-10618d86-2776-5cce-97a6-7ca9e920abd5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ff82ea5-a53e-581b-bf6e-70bfe7b8756b" :answer/id #uuid "4ff82ea5-a53e-581b-bf6e-70bfe7b8756b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{a}^{5}+3{a}^{2}+6{a}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4cfe73b4-b0e8-50ac-850e-f133bc075de3" :answer/id #uuid "4cfe73b4-b0e8-50ac-850e-f133bc075de3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{a}^{6}+3{a}^{3}+6a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f80efb83-27d0-51e9-bdfb-27593f4de169" :answer/id #uuid "f80efb83-27d0-51e9-bdfb-27593f4de169" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{a}^{6}+3{a}^{4}+6{a}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47ed6dd6-b0d1-5887-8326-53ee4a3b117a" :answer/id #uuid "47ed6dd6-b0d1-5887-8326-53ee4a3b117a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{a}^{6}+2{a}^{4}+5{a}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10618d86-2776-5cce-97a6-7ca9e920abd5" :answer/id #uuid "10618d86-2776-5cce-97a6-7ca9e920abd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}^{2}-3{a}^{4}+{a}^{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064216 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a0223a5d-a1d6-5c40-af63-e8dfd73551f8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a0223a5d-a1d6-5c40-af63-e8dfd73551f8" :question/id #uuid "a0223a5d-a1d6-5c40-af63-e8dfd73551f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-111117" :question/problem "$\\frac{x}{2}(6-10{x}^{3})=$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply each term inside the parentheses by the term outside the parentheses, simplify using the rules of exponents, and then we add the results together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}(6-10{x}^{3}) & = \\\\ (\\frac{x}{2})(6)+(\\frac{x}{2})(-10{x}^{3}) & = \\\\ (\\frac{1}{2}x)(6)+(\\frac{1}{2}x)(-10{x}^{3}) & = \\\\ (\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6)x+(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-10))(x\\cdot {x}^{3}) & = \\\\ (3)x+(-5)({x}^{1+3}) & = \\\\ 3x-5{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cc8bf450-8384-5183-8fd7-ee109eb1c278"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cc8bf450-8384-5183-8fd7-ee109eb1c278" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc8bf450-8384-5183-8fd7-ee109eb1c278" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3f663968-9914-51d2-a0d5-0de18327bcb2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c9c56fc1-b117-576b-81a6-2f4abdab9754" "answer-3f663968-9914-51d2-a0d5-0de18327bcb2" "answer-aa8be593-a930-5092-b401-4276e53f4bb9" "answer-f6bfd523-eab9-5a44-b230-8dd48c8d9b55" "answer-aab4c61d-684a-5773-b4d6-164888798bb8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9c56fc1-b117-576b-81a6-2f4abdab9754" :answer/id #uuid "c9c56fc1-b117-576b-81a6-2f4abdab9754" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3x}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f663968-9914-51d2-a0d5-0de18327bcb2" :answer/id #uuid "3f663968-9914-51d2-a0d5-0de18327bcb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-5{x}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa8be593-a930-5092-b401-4276e53f4bb9" :answer/id #uuid "aa8be593-a930-5092-b401-4276e53f4bb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6bfd523-eab9-5a44-b230-8dd48c8d9b55" :answer/id #uuid "f6bfd523-eab9-5a44-b230-8dd48c8d9b55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x+5{x}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aab4c61d-684a-5773-b4d6-164888798bb8" :answer/id #uuid "aab4c61d-684a-5773-b4d6-164888798bb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3x}{2}-5{x}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-d65a0de1-92e1-56c5-b358-49f6ba21fa25" :activity/id #uuid "d65a0de1-92e1-56c5-b358-49f6ba21fa25" :activity/title "The Distributive Law for Polynomials" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048422 :activity/course 17592186046648 :activity/steps ["step-0bc8636c-0807-5847-a5a8-7748bf0a3cfb" "step-73a8d1dc-0fad-55c8-9ef4-adcb5e444d92" "step-fef1509a-8ac4-5f19-b17b-2194e4983c02"] :activity/first-step "step-0bc8636c-0807-5847-a5a8-7748bf0a3cfb" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-0bc8636c-0807-5847-a5a8-7748bf0a3cfb" :step/id #uuid "0bc8636c-0807-5847-a5a8-7748bf0a3cfb" :step/content "question-9cfc88f5-5c61-5b90-beb5-64a3476a024f" :step/next "step-73a8d1dc-0fad-55c8-9ef4-adcb5e444d92" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-73a8d1dc-0fad-55c8-9ef4-adcb5e444d92" :step/id #uuid "73a8d1dc-0fad-55c8-9ef4-adcb5e444d92" :step/content "question-aad55e06-4983-5ff1-b72a-41466f8cbb81" :step/next "step-fef1509a-8ac4-5f19-b17b-2194e4983c02" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fef1509a-8ac4-5f19-b17b-2194e4983c02" :step/id #uuid "fef1509a-8ac4-5f19-b17b-2194e4983c02" :step/content "question-a0223a5d-a1d6-5c40-af63-e8dfd73551f8" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186117475 :answer-field/choices 17592186117476] [:db/retract 17592186117475 :answer-field/choices 17592186117478] [:db/retract 17592186117475 :answer-field/choices 17592186117479] [:db/retract 17592186117475 :answer-field/choices 17592186117480] {:db/id 17592186120219 :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(6,0,2)$ and $B(1,1,3)$, and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨3,1,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨3,1,-2⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,1,3⟩-⟨6,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $a=⟨6,0,2⟩$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\ r & =⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨3,1,-2⟩+t⟨-5,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186117475 :answer-field/correct "answer-e994da9e-a986-53ac-b530-86db42005ecc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e994da9e-a986-53ac-b530-86db42005ecc" "answer-6ea6b719-d65e-5d67-8999-88b13c999f44" "answer-54e5a00f-239b-539d-9f9b-5957f11c633b" "answer-6842561b-d1ec-5753-b48f-a0a96c8d26d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e994da9e-a986-53ac-b530-86db42005ecc" :answer/id #uuid "e994da9e-a986-53ac-b530-86db42005ecc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨3,1,-2⟩+t⟨-5,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ea6b719-d65e-5d67-8999-88b13c999f44" :answer/id #uuid "6ea6b719-d65e-5d67-8999-88b13c999f44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨3,1,-2⟩+t⟨1,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54e5a00f-239b-539d-9f9b-5957f11c633b" :answer/id #uuid "54e5a00f-239b-539d-9f9b-5957f11c633b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨3,1,-2⟩+t⟨6,0,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6842561b-d1ec-5753-b48f-a0a96c8d26d9" :answer/id #uuid "6842561b-d1ec-5753-b48f-a0a96c8d26d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨6,0,2⟩+t⟨1,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119934 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7340caf5-7f57-5ed9-b918-72cd124f498f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7340caf5-7f57-5ed9-b918-72cd124f498f" :question/id #uuid "7340caf5-7f57-5ed9-b918-72cd124f498f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70975" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨0,8,-1⟩+t⟨-1,1,7⟩+s⟨3,-5,1⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-1,1,7⟩$ and $w=⟨3,-5,1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =36i+22j+2k \\\\  & =⟨36,22,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨36,22,2⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8bf0e22c-7173-584a-ae1b-a7c0bd01e586"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8bf0e22c-7173-584a-ae1b-a7c0bd01e586" :answer-field/id #uuid "8bf0e22c-7173-584a-ae1b-a7c0bd01e586" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a52411c7-786b-5482-9881-e7a8a452b864" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5ee143c1-2d22-5a6b-8226-53337f0c9aa5" "answer-426d2f86-6e44-5b72-8222-a1d8c826de45" "answer-81af70fa-ea19-54cc-83e0-b0a21fab95e2" "answer-87ba8eac-d335-511b-94ef-29242597cc39" "answer-a52411c7-786b-5482-9881-e7a8a452b864"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ee143c1-2d22-5a6b-8226-53337f0c9aa5" :answer/id #uuid "5ee143c1-2d22-5a6b-8226-53337f0c9aa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,1,7⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-426d2f86-6e44-5b72-8222-a1d8c826de45" :answer/id #uuid "426d2f86-6e44-5b72-8222-a1d8c826de45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-3,-5,7⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81af70fa-ea19-54cc-83e0-b0a21fab95e2" :answer/id #uuid "81af70fa-ea19-54cc-83e0-b0a21fab95e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-34,-22,8⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87ba8eac-d335-511b-94ef-29242597cc39" :answer/id #uuid "87ba8eac-d335-511b-94ef-29242597cc39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,-5,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a52411c7-786b-5482-9881-e7a8a452b864" :answer/id #uuid "a52411c7-786b-5482-9881-e7a8a452b864" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨36,22,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-76f4a73c-4542-5db3-9e7f-34252998a80c" :activity/id #uuid "76f4a73c-4542-5db3-9e7f-34252998a80c" :activity/title "The Parametric Equations of a Plane" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050308 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-ab3c66e4-605d-5530-9113-4164fad58316" "step-07ae2f09-fe9e-5ba9-a0d7-b2c82c644d07" "step-887eff77-49fb-5aec-b491-643d8fc3ea4c" "step-8eaa6107-75a7-5433-8966-ae16f584399a" "step-2ca5f55d-d481-5b90-9268-9016376d2ff8"] :activity/first-step "step-ab3c66e4-605d-5530-9113-4164fad58316" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-ab3c66e4-605d-5530-9113-4164fad58316" :step/id #uuid "ab3c66e4-605d-5530-9113-4164fad58316" :step/content 17592186120219 :step/next "step-07ae2f09-fe9e-5ba9-a0d7-b2c82c644d07" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-07ae2f09-fe9e-5ba9-a0d7-b2c82c644d07" :step/id #uuid "07ae2f09-fe9e-5ba9-a0d7-b2c82c644d07" :step/content 17592186311921 :step/next "step-887eff77-49fb-5aec-b491-643d8fc3ea4c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-887eff77-49fb-5aec-b491-643d8fc3ea4c" :step/id #uuid "887eff77-49fb-5aec-b491-643d8fc3ea4c" :step/content "question-7340caf5-7f57-5ed9-b918-72cd124f498f" :step/next "step-8eaa6107-75a7-5433-8966-ae16f584399a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8eaa6107-75a7-5433-8966-ae16f584399a" :step/id #uuid "8eaa6107-75a7-5433-8966-ae16f584399a" :step/content 17592186393064 :step/next "step-2ca5f55d-d481-5b90-9268-9016376d2ff8" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2ca5f55d-d481-5b90-9268-9016376d2ff8" :step/id #uuid "2ca5f55d-d481-5b90-9268-9016376d2ff8" :step/content 17592186398347 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142780 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7a9fb5ec-479f-5a41-8212-79254e42e93a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7a9fb5ec-479f-5a41-8212-79254e42e93a" :question/id #uuid "7a9fb5ec-479f-5a41-8212-79254e42e93a" :question/math-academy-id "q-134277" :question/problem "Peter, Steve, Chelsea, and Laura each bought $3$ ounces of gummies and $4$ ounces of chocolates. In total, they bought$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$ounces of candy." :question/worked-solution "We must write and evaluate an expression representing the total amount of candy.\n\nSince each of them bought $3$ ounces of gummies and $4$ ounces of chocolates, the amount of candy each person bought, in ounces, is:\n\n$$\n{{3}_{⏟}}_{\\text{gummies}}+{{4}_{⏟}}_{\\text{chocolates}}\n$$\n\nSince *each* person purchased this amount of candy, and there are $4$ people, we must multiply the amount of candy by $4.$ Therefore, the total amount of candy is:\n\n$$\n{{(3+4)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{each person}}\\times {{4}_{⏟}}_{\\text{people}}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the expression, we follow the order of operations with parentheses.\n\nFirst, we perform the operations inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+4)\\times 4 & =(3+4)\\times 4 \\\\  & =7\\times 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply:\n\n$$\n7\\times 4=28\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bc0b31b7-280c-571d-99c0-05af9c3c0458"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bc0b31b7-280c-571d-99c0-05af9c3c0458" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc0b31b7-280c-571d-99c0-05af9c3c0458" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-af949fa7-a0e1-56e7-9dec-9a12fe81fc13" :answer-field/choices ["answer-af949fa7-a0e1-56e7-9dec-9a12fe81fc13"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af949fa7-a0e1-56e7-9dec-9a12fe81fc13" :answer/id #uuid "af949fa7-a0e1-56e7-9dec-9a12fe81fc13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059859 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-83ea9ab0-b2f6-54ee-a35a-5ac8d6525a5a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-83ea9ab0-b2f6-54ee-a35a-5ac8d6525a5a" :question/id #uuid "83ea9ab0-b2f6-54ee-a35a-5ac8d6525a5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-134278" :question/problem "There are $14$ boxes of lollipops in stock, each box containing $22$ lollipops. Therefore, there are $\\,${{field-1}}\n$\\,$lollipops in the store." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total number of lollipops, we need to multiply $14$ by $22.$\n\nSo, we write it this way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  &  &  & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the ones:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \\boxed{0}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}14\\times 2=28\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply the tens:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{0}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}14\\times 20=280\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{0}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}28+280=308\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $14\\times 22=308.$\n\nTherefore, there are $308$ lollipops in total." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9a683d32-1f62-5466-96f6-53c5085243be"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9a683d32-1f62-5466-96f6-53c5085243be" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a683d32-1f62-5466-96f6-53c5085243be" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ae0c95fd-0ecb-511d-bd41-1811494e1952" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ae0c95fd-0ecb-511d-bd41-1811494e1952"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae0c95fd-0ecb-511d-bd41-1811494e1952" :answer/id #uuid "ae0c95fd-0ecb-511d-bd41-1811494e1952" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "308" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073842 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-dfff5d32-78f7-5797-b312-14bdc373c270"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-dfff5d32-78f7-5797-b312-14bdc373c270" :question/id #uuid "dfff5d32-78f7-5797-b312-14bdc373c270" :question/math-academy-id "q-134279" :question/problem "There are $308$ lollipops at the store. The store manager wants to make packages containing $4$ lollipops each. In total, he can make$\\,${{field-1}}\n$\\,$packages." :question/worked-solution "We know that there are $308$ lollipops in total. Since each package must contain $4$ lollipops,the store manager can make $308÷4$ packages.\n\nWe start by writing down the question using long division notation:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{3\\,\\phantom{|}0\\,\\phantom{|}8}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNotice that $3$ (the number of hundreds in $308$) is less than the divisor $4.$ Therefore, we should consider both the hundreds and tens:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{3\\,\\phantom{|}0\\,\\phantom{|}8}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$↓$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Divide: $30÷4=7\\,\\text{R}\\,2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Write over tens: $7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Multiply: $4\\times 7=28$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Subtract: $30-28=2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Bring down: $8$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNext, we consider the ones:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{3\\,\\phantom{|}0\\,\\phantom{|}8}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\boxed{\\text{0}}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Divide: $28÷4=7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Write over ones: $7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Multiply: $4\\times 7=28$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Subtract: $28-28=0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe get the remainder $0$, so the division is done.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n308÷4=77.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dc56acdc-bb5e-585d-b688-0b28d6cc7c09"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dc56acdc-bb5e-585d-b688-0b28d6cc7c09" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc56acdc-bb5e-585d-b688-0b28d6cc7c09" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8340c0b0-5f9e-5edc-936d-7a447e4e9434" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8340c0b0-5f9e-5edc-936d-7a447e4e9434"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8340c0b0-5f9e-5edc-936d-7a447e4e9434" :answer/id #uuid "8340c0b0-5f9e-5edc-936d-7a447e4e9434" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "77" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073698 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-24d13ec7-deb1-5d3a-8434-3206289f496e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-24d13ec7-deb1-5d3a-8434-3206289f496e" :question/id #uuid "24d13ec7-deb1-5d3a-8434-3206289f496e" :question/math-academy-id "q-134280" :question/problem "John bought $2$ pounds of chocolate almonds while Rose bought $\\frac{7}{5}$ pound of the same product. How many chocolate almonds did they buy altogether? Express your final answer as a mixed number.\n\nThey bought$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$pounds of chocolate almonds." :question/worked-solution "To determine the amount of chocolate almonds they bought in total, we have to calculate the following sum:\n\n$$\n2+\\frac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nTo add $2$ and $\\frac{7}{5},$ we need to express the whole number $2$ as an equivalent fraction with a denominator of $5.$\n\nFirst, we write $2$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nThen we put this fraction over a denominator of $5$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 5}{1\\times 5}=\\frac{10}{5}\n$$\n\nSo now, we have to find:\n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{5}+\\frac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nTo add two fractions with like denominators, we add the numerators and keep the denominators the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{5}+\\frac{7}{5}=\\frac{10+7}{5}=\\frac{17}{5}\n$$\n\nExpressing our answer as a mixed number, we have\n\n$$\n17÷5=3\\,\\text{R}\\,2=3\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, John and Rose bought $3\\frac{2}{5}$ pounds of chocolate almonds." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-50f9e705-c005-5353-94c6-f53555ea549b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-50f9e705-c005-5353-94c6-f53555ea549b" :answer-field/id #uuid "50f9e705-c005-5353-94c6-f53555ea549b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-722bea08-8936-52a3-9467-fcfbfe46f1cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-722bea08-8936-52a3-9467-fcfbfe46f1cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-722bea08-8936-52a3-9467-fcfbfe46f1cb" :answer/id #uuid "722bea08-8936-52a3-9467-fcfbfe46f1cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073826 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-40b45065-d83b-509a-aac4-0020a7f5f19d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-40b45065-d83b-509a-aac4-0020a7f5f19d" :question/id #uuid "40b45065-d83b-509a-aac4-0020a7f5f19d" :question/math-academy-id "q-134281" :question/problem "Of the $2$ pounds of chocolate almonds that John bought, he gave his cousin Angela $\\frac{5}{6}$ pounds. As a mixed number, John had{{field-1}}\n$\\,$pounds of chocolate almonds remaining." :question/worked-solution "To find out how many chocolate almonds John had left, we must calculate the difference $2-\\frac{5}{6}.$\n\nTo subtract $\\frac{5}{6}$ from $2,$ we need to express the whole number $2$ as an equivalent fraction with a denominator of $6.$\n\nFirst, we write $2$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nThen, we put this fraction over a denominator of $6$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 6}{1\\times 6}=\\frac{12}{6}\n$$\n\nSo now, we have to find:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{6}-\\frac{5}{6}\n$$\n\nTo subtract two fractions with like denominators, we subtract the numerators and keep the denominators the same. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{6}-\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{12-5}{6}=\\frac{7}{6}\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n7÷6=1\\,\\text{R}\\,1=1\\,\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, John has $1\\,\\frac{1}{6}$ pounds of chocolate almonds left." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5993c571-c20a-58b1-882a-ac3ee5b1add0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5993c571-c20a-58b1-882a-ac3ee5b1add0" :answer-field/id #uuid "5993c571-c20a-58b1-882a-ac3ee5b1add0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-caf57738-44c8-587f-972e-708843835102" :answer-field/choices ["answer-caf57738-44c8-587f-972e-708843835102"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-caf57738-44c8-587f-972e-708843835102" :answer/id #uuid "caf57738-44c8-587f-972e-708843835102" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198431 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bc49bd25-7e09-53de-af63-f601d564b8e6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-bc49bd25-7e09-53de-af63-f601d564b8e6" :question/id #uuid "bc49bd25-7e09-53de-af63-f601d564b8e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-134282" :question/problem "After Angela takes her share of John's chocolate almonds, the weight of John's remaining chocolate almonds is$\\,${{field-1}}\n$\\,$than the weight of Rose's chocolate almonds because $1\\frac{1}{6}$\n{{field-2}} $\\frac{7}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "John has $1\\frac{1}{6}$ pounds of chocolate almonds remaining, and Rose has $\\frac{7}{5}$ pounds of this product.\n\nWe cannot compare the fractions directly as they don't have a common denominator.\n\nWe can make a common denominator of $6\\times 5=30.$\n\nTo put $1\\frac{1}{6}$ over a denominator of $30,$ we first convert to an improper fraction and then multiply the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n1\\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{7}{6}=\\frac{7\\times 5}{6\\times 5}=\\frac{35}{30}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{7}{5}$ over a denominator of $30,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{5}=\\frac{7\\times 6}{5\\times 6}=\\frac{42}{30}\n$$\n\nWe can now compare the fractions $\\frac{35}{30}$ and $\\frac{42}{30}$ by looking at the numerators only.\n\nSince $35<42,$ the correct statement must be:\n\n$$\n\\frac{35}{30}<\\frac{42}{30}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is\n\n> \"After Angela takes her part of John's chocolate almonds, the weight of John's remaining chocolate almonds is $<$ than the weight of Rose's chocolate almonds because $1\\frac{1}{6}<\\frac{7}{5}.$\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-28f14609-5ba0-5c3c-bd50-2e1412d984d2" "answer-field-7051bced-174c-578a-b9d0-e93a60d7a4ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-28f14609-5ba0-5c3c-bd50-2e1412d984d2" :answer-field/id #uuid "28f14609-5ba0-5c3c-bd50-2e1412d984d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-45ef829c-c63f-5803-b57d-7b3406727070" :answer-field/choices ["answer-45ef829c-c63f-5803-b57d-7b3406727070"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45ef829c-c63f-5803-b57d-7b3406727070" :answer/id #uuid "45ef829c-c63f-5803-b57d-7b3406727070" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "less" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7051bced-174c-578a-b9d0-e93a60d7a4ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "7051bced-174c-578a-b9d0-e93a60d7a4ad" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-009416f5-95d3-521b-972f-c0312d6dc1e1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-009416f5-95d3-521b-972f-c0312d6dc1e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-009416f5-95d3-521b-972f-c0312d6dc1e1" :answer/id #uuid "009416f5-95d3-521b-972f-c0312d6dc1e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142796 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7b9cad24-adba-5e25-92cf-4f2a7c2a1894"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7b9cad24-adba-5e25-92cf-4f2a7c2a1894" :question/id #uuid "7b9cad24-adba-5e25-92cf-4f2a7c2a1894" :question/math-academy-id "q-134283" :question/problem "Rose decides to eat $\\frac{2}{5}$ of her chocolate almonds. How many pounds of almonds does she decide to eat?\n\n*Remember that Rose has $\\frac{7}{5}$ of a pound of chocolate almonds.*\n\nRose decides to eat\n{{field-1}}\npounds of chocolate almonds." :question/worked-solution "We know that Rose has $\\frac{7}{5}$ of a pound of chocolate almonds.\n\nTo calculate the fraction of a whole pound that Rose decides to eat, we need to multiply $\\frac{2}{5}$ by $\\frac{7}{5}.$\n\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{7}{5}=\\frac{2\\times 7}{5\\times 5}=\\frac{14}{25}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Rose decides to eat $\\frac{14}{25}$ pounds of chocolate almonds." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c6b96e89-e07b-5a12-a9c0-374702448788"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c6b96e89-e07b-5a12-a9c0-374702448788" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6b96e89-e07b-5a12-a9c0-374702448788" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-976747e5-d3e2-516c-b98a-7e5317a01151" :answer-field/choices ["answer-976747e5-d3e2-516c-b98a-7e5317a01151"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-976747e5-d3e2-516c-b98a-7e5317a01151" :answer/id #uuid "976747e5-d3e2-516c-b98a-7e5317a01151" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "multistep-3ef56e99-ee02-5a7a-b434-af1fab1ad5e2" :multistep/id #uuid "3ef56e99-ee02-5a7a-b434-af1fab1ad5e2" :multistep/context "A store in a small town sells candy." :multistep/steps ["step-2fff77ad-eb75-5f8e-852c-f1c3e4893795" "step-0e171485-6b08-5e96-a554-7c7599eb6753" "step-f5c45b23-6c86-5659-b613-9bc872822ef5" "step-3611c6bb-60dd-5de2-8451-66acc526a034" "step-e115a753-202a-55ac-9233-a46aa989055a" "step-6845889e-08d1-56a7-9dbe-32e13043ea52" "step-09fbdd8d-ce54-5956-a8aa-a99300b51219"] :multistep/first-step "step-2fff77ad-eb75-5f8e-852c-f1c3e4893795" :db/ensure [:multistep/validate]} {:db/id "step-2fff77ad-eb75-5f8e-852c-f1c3e4893795" :step/id #uuid "2fff77ad-eb75-5f8e-852c-f1c3e4893795" :step/content "question-7a9fb5ec-479f-5a41-8212-79254e42e93a" :step/next "step-0e171485-6b08-5e96-a554-7c7599eb6753" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0e171485-6b08-5e96-a554-7c7599eb6753" :step/id #uuid "0e171485-6b08-5e96-a554-7c7599eb6753" :step/content "question-83ea9ab0-b2f6-54ee-a35a-5ac8d6525a5a" :step/next "step-f5c45b23-6c86-5659-b613-9bc