 "question-8633e974-6d10-58b7-b01c-e86dcc646ae6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166665 :question/worked-solution "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](images/60/6044f7e9a7a3e784da6affc47c4cfcedce461feb44057992f39fd3154e5cb846.svg)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](images/d4/d4788968ba8347e6288028e679a0df0c3629c292aaca4552293fc6f9380486ef.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =f(3) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}(\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166828 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-458360eb-fd03-5244-aa64-17cd1909b422" "question-c5de4d6c-cfeb-57f1-bb0f-e9ef45447169" "question-4c144938-ebf0-5b6b-9305-5aba70df7465" "question-976a3fe7-7c3e-53a0-9a3a-1795aa3e30b7" "question-17f155c2-ce06-547c-8fc5-5b0b0c48ed1f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166666 :question/worked-solution "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](images/f6/f6da43d5d0276991429f04048f3ea4e7ec2b4d9727abc71f4d7879cefd71797b.svg)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 37\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](images/bc/bcba51c019bfe72f14e0fb7d6465abf3595b03c8e70598231934f5166393873b.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4}{7})}^{0}(\\frac{3}{7})+{(\\frac{4}{7})}^{1}(\\frac{3}{7})+{(\\frac{4}{7})}^{2}(\\frac{3}{7})+{(\\frac{4}{7})}^{3}(\\frac{3}{7}) \\\\  & ≈0.893\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto  $3$ decimal places." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166829 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ebe82800-a8b2-58e9-ab4c-047410ac5d4f" "question-e519920d-4b78-559e-a669-c1163fd46764" "question-89650cb6-ad4a-5818-b55e-8a9dde9d78b4" "question-5e3a6ede-352d-5bbc-898c-f52f077d9252" "question-2f7bb618-1c74-5b28-8d56-423cfe55dc4d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166667 :question/worked-solution "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](images/8f/8fe2487af4333bae81059a2ab221b3988bbdf27f4f51521683addd789c31a4b9.svg)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 15\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](images/a4/a44212ab1418417646876630a4cea241bfefaf063b26251dc5f157824cc4805d.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 3) & =P(X\\in \\{2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4}{5})}^{1}(\\frac{1}{5})+{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{125}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166830 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-409b1f60-69c1-5499-92f9-7ef6676bbb2d" "question-04c3981e-56b1-51ed-b49e-4d2d764aacc9" "question-f9e4e9da-f36b-5b4a-91a7-731a48c88c99" "question-c2bbdab6-51f8-5199-a746-5b96164dbacd" "question-075d366c-d06a-5f72-a1db-49d33772eb88"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166668 :question/worked-solution "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](images/0d/0d3d01e8f77c51e75d7dfce4ef2b60e8a61be89eaf752b2203857d97e77c6127.svg)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 56\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](images/db/db0084ae705309592c8d309304e26a46ecde6e6a1b85ef07b57b6f1a394f26fa.svg)\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X > 2.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{6})}^{0}(\\frac{5}{6})+{(\\frac{1}{6})}^{1}(\\frac{5}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{35}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-3c3e7bcc-b40d-5576-a6ae-56d69405dfc0" :question/id #uuid "3c3e7bcc-b40d-5576-a6ae-56d69405dfc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-130033" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.45),$ compute $P(X=4).$  Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.45),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(0.55)}^{x-1}(0.45), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4) & =f(4) \\\\  & ={(0.55)}^{3}(0.45) \\\\  & ≈0.0749.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-505f0222-4cef-53e2-a6b9-3e430e0cccd9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-505f0222-4cef-53e2-a6b9-3e430e0cccd9" :answer-field/id #uuid "505f0222-4cef-53e2-a6b9-3e430e0cccd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-12719200-e104-56e8-b712-c638a73fe46f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-924cd6fa-d634-5f0d-8aca-01b2e778a480" "answer-73793f7d-9072-5da6-abd4-390066e06095" "answer-12719200-e104-56e8-b712-c638a73fe46f" "answer-c88e1276-0a5c-53af-a35b-40bf38708c04" "answer-5d21d304-740b-5376-a2c8-3fcb5c2851e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-924cd6fa-d634-5f0d-8aca-01b2e778a480" :answer/id #uuid "924cd6fa-d634-5f0d-8aca-01b2e778a480" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0412" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73793f7d-9072-5da6-abd4-390066e06095" :answer/id #uuid "73793f7d-9072-5da6-abd4-390066e06095" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0501" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12719200-e104-56e8-b712-c638a73fe46f" :answer/id #uuid "12719200-e104-56e8-b712-c638a73fe46f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0749" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c88e1276-0a5c-53af-a35b-40bf38708c04" :answer/id #uuid "c88e1276-0a5c-53af-a35b-40bf38708c04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0915" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d21d304-740b-5376-a2c8-3fcb5c2851e6" :answer/id #uuid "5d21d304-740b-5376-a2c8-3fcb5c2851e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1664" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f5dba093-2258-5290-b7aa-4504e51efcbb" :question/id #uuid "f5dba093-2258-5290-b7aa-4504e51efcbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-97131" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{1}{4}),$ compute $P(X=3).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{1}{4}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x-1}(\\frac{1}{4}), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =f(3) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5dbf1190-a21a-5af1-a02b-35bdfc87730d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5dbf1190-a21a-5af1-a02b-35bdfc87730d" :answer-field/id #uuid "5dbf1190-a21a-5af1-a02b-35bdfc87730d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-033c65a9-0b6e-5617-bdf6-d1c79c11ea62" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dff4f121-9d79-55a3-91b8-351004a0cd79" "answer-f1f01b94-5019-585f-8fe7-9ef5261221ae" "answer-2dcd0755-ff5f-51d8