ligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1548ad33-92ee-5cc7-a272-b792c434a1c4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1548ad33-92ee-5cc7-a272-b792c434a1c4" :answer-field/id #uuid "1548ad33-92ee-5cc7-a272-b792c434a1c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-07837112-8580-50b9-aa46-6f6bfd4a1983" :answer-field/choices ["answer-07837112-8580-50b9-aa46-6f6bfd4a1983"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07837112-8580-50b9-aa46-6f6bfd4a1983" :answer/id #uuid "07837112-8580-50b9-aa46-6f6bfd4a1983" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0156" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ddebff9a-c321-5053-81a7-09bc2befcfb5" :question/id #uuid "ddebff9a-c321-5053-81a7-09bc2befcfb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-130032" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.7),$ compute $P(X=4).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.7),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(0.3)}^{x-1}(0.7), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4) & =f(4) \\\\  & ={(0.3)}^{3}(0.7) \\\\  & =0.0189.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d2f3772d-82b4-52de-abe3-8e3cd1b9192d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d2f3772d-82b4-52de-abe3-8e3cd1b9192d" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2f3772d-82b4-52de-abe3-8e3cd1b9192d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d97464cd-bf5a-577a-9847-a99a3c83a3fc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9ef3d34e-9394-51e7-ab15-87526ccf7d58" "answer-a4b66f29-5a42-52a3-be66-da30a8d25610" "an